.TH GCC-AR 1 "" "Peios" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gcc-ar, gcc-nm, gcc-ranlib \- invoke GNU binary utilities with the GCC LTO plugin
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gcc-ar
.RI [ "-B prefix" ] " ar-arguments ..."
.br
.B gcc-nm
.RI [ "-B prefix" ] " nm-arguments ..."
.br
.B gcc-ranlib
.RI [ "-B prefix" ] " ranlib-arguments ..."
.SH DESCRIPTION
These GCC wrappers invoke the corresponding GNU binary utility with the
link-time optimization (LTO) plugin belonging to this compiler installation.
Use them when inspecting or archiving objects produced with GCC's
.B -flto
option, particularly when the objects do not also contain native machine code.
.PP
Arguments are forwarded to the underlying utility, with the plugin options
added by the wrapper. The optional
.B -B
prefix changes the wrapper's search path for tools and the plugin.
Target-prefixed names provide the same interface for the named target.
.SH OPTIONS
See the corresponding utility manual for archive operations, symbol-display
options, archive-index operations, and their exit status conventions.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ar (1),
.BR nm (1),
.BR ranlib (1),
.BR gcc (1)
.PP
The GCC manual's link-time optimization documentation describes using these
wrappers with static libraries.
